{"id": 4383063, "name": "Fitzsimons v. The Guanahani Company", "name_abbreviation": "Fitzsimons v. Guanahani Co.", "decision_date": "1885-07-30", "docket_number": "No. 1738", "first_page": "603", "last_page": "604", "citations": [{"type": "official", "cite": "23 S.C. 603"}], "court": {"name_abbreviation": "S.C.", "id": 8894, "name": "Supreme Court of South Carolina"}, "jurisdiction": {"id": 59, "name_long": "South Carolina", "name": "S.C."}, "cites_to": [{"cite": "16 S. C., 192", "category": "reporters:state", "reporter": "S.C.", "case_ids": [4377718], "opinion_index": 0, "case_paths": ["/sc/16/0192-01"]}], "analysis": {"cardinality": 127, "char_count": 1432, "ocr_confidence": 0.476, "pagerank": {"raw": 4.03580807328026e-08, "percentile": 0.1494733862862275}, "sha256": "c675567cded69bd179018adb42da3f6fb0d02dd8f87fe6fc62704c31c8d92030", "simhash": "1:4274ef8f889ade27", "word_count": 249}, "last_updated": "2024-02-27T16:23:33.634210+00:00", "provenance": {"date_added": "2019-08-29", "source": "Harvard", "batch": "2018"}, "casebody": {"judges": [], "parties": ["Fitzsimons v. The Guanahani Company."], "opinions": [{"text": "Opinion by\nMr. Chief -Justice Simpson,\nThis case was tried upon the same pleadings and evidence as at the first trial of the case, reported 16 S. C., 192. The Circuit Judge (Hudson), feeling bound by the statement of this court on that appeal, that \u201cplaintiff had based his right to sue on the ground that he was an inspector under the statute of Georgia, and that the action could not be sustained under said statute,\u201d charged the jury that if they found that the services had been rendered outside of that State, the plaintiff could not recover. On appeal the court say that the Circuit Judge overlooked the fact that while this expression was found in that opinion, yet that this was not the question raised in the appeal, nor was it the point upon which the judgment was there reversed; nor was the second opinion of this court in this case (21 S. (7., 599) brought to the judge\u2019s attention, in which, this court attempted to correct the misapprehension as to the point decided in the first, and which gave rise to the demurrer at the second trial.\nWhile the plaintiff cannot recover for services in this State under any contract raised by a Georgia statute, he could for services rendered at a stipulated price agreed upon between the parties, independent of such statute.\nJudgment reversed.", "type": "majority", "author": "Mr. Chief -Justice Simpson,"}], "attorneys": ["W. J. Verdier, for appellant. William Elliott, contra."], "corrections": "", "head_matter": "No. 1738.\nFitzsimons v. The Guanahani Company.\nApril Term, 1885.\nJuly 30, 1885.\nW. J. Verdier, for appellant. William Elliott, contra."}, "file_name": "0603-02", "first_page_order": 611, "last_page_order": 612}